# this is the root level gitignore, covers stuff shared across the whole repo that the six
# per service gitignores below do not already handle on their own

# just in case aws cli creds ever end up sitting locally in the repo folder, never want these committed
.aws/

# terraform keeps its downloaded provider/module cache and real state locally, state especially can
# contain resource ids and sometimes secrets, none of this belongs in git, this is why terraform.tfvars
# with the real db password gets kept out even though a placeholder version could theoretically be shared
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
*.tfvars
override.tf
override.tf.json

# everyone's editor of choice leaves its own folder behind, ignoring the common ones so this
# does not turn into a fight over whose ide config gets committed
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# windows and mac both leave these behind when you browse a folder, pure clutter, never useful in git
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local secrets live in .env (Twilio account sid/auth token, SendGrid api key, and anything else
# added later). Never committed - the tracked .env.example carries the variable NAMES only, so a
# fresh clone knows what to set without any real value ever reaching git.
.env
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Spring's convention for a local-only profile. Anything in a file named like this is assumed to
# hold real credentials, so it stays out of git across every service.
**/application-local.yml
**/application-local.yaml
**/application-local.properties
**/application-secrets.yml

# a k8s Secret manifest with real values filled in - the tracked k8s/02-secrets.yaml holds
# placeholders only, so any *.local.yaml copy of it is the one carrying the real thing
k8s/*.local.yaml

# private keys and certificates, whatever tool drops them
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks

# personal local planning doc for a future AWS deploy session - not meant to be tracked/shared
aws-deployment-plan/

# stray maven debug output, not meant to be tracked
maven-debug.log